Package: CBAMMR
Type: Package
Title: Comprehensive Bayesian and Advanced Meta-Analysis Methods in R
Version: 8.12.0
Date: 2025-11-05
Authors@R: c(
    person("Mahmood", "Developer", email = "mahmood726@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Claude", "AI", role = "ctb")
    )
Description: Revolutionary intelligent meta-analysis system that removes researcher degrees
    of freedom and prevents p-hacking through automated, data-driven decisions. Features
    cbamm_auto() - the world's first fully automated meta-analysis function that detects data type,
    calculates appropriate effect sizes, selects optimal methods based on data characteristics,
    assesses heterogeneity and publication bias, runs sensitivity analyses, provides
    evidence-based recommendations, and generates journal-quality R Markdown results sections
    ready for direct manuscript inclusion - all without subjective choices. Also includes ALL capabilities
    from metafor and meta packages: complete effect size calculation (40+ measures), all meta-analysis
    types (binary, continuous, proportions, rates, correlations), comprehensive heterogeneity toolkit
    (Q, I², H², tau², Bayes factors, R², decomposition), model selection (AIC/BIC/AICc, CV, LRT),
    complete publication bias assessment (7 methods: Egger, Begg, trim-and-fill, PET-PEESE, selection
    models, p-curve, funnel tests), pairwise effects, transportability weighting, robust variance
    estimation, multivariate meta-analysis, Bayesian methods (bootstrap, MCMC), distribution-free
    methods (permutation, bootstrap, quantile regression), clinical decision tools (EVPI, decision
    curves, NNT, treatment rankings), complete metafor/meta plotting integration (10 plot types),
    unified interface with batch generation, 10 example datasets, and interactive GUI. Standardizes
    methodology and ensures reproducibility. The ultimate solution for evidence-based meta-analysis.
